[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one bug: the parser reads day-first dates month first. Read by
tenant, channel and body, its reports hold three problems with three different fixes.
Each now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
Fixing the parser alone leaves two of these open. Do not close the tickets below with it.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first. Our tenants write the day
  first, so day and month swap (7 April → 4 July). App, email and the booking-v2 form.
- **`hint`**: booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type month first,
  as told; the form reads the tenant's way, day first. Same symptom as `parser`, but only
  through the booking-v3 form, and a parser fix does not touch it.
- **`one-day-shift`**: the date moves by one day, or differs per attendee time zone ("Lisbon
  got Tuesday, Toronto got Monday"). A time-zone bug, not a swap. The desk already listed these
  in `desk-notes.json`; until now they were filed under `parser`.

## How the reports were placed

- One report per id: the export repeats some rows (`uniqueById`).
- The cause follows the tenant (`causes.ts`, `locales.ts`), not intake's tag. Intake guesses
  from the reporter's browser and disagrees with the tenant on dozens of reports.
- The desk's `oneDayMove` notes take a report out of `parser` into `one-day-shift`.

## Why they were merged

Triage merges on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). A
subject says "wrong day"; it does not say which way in or which form. Three causes, one subject.

